From b71a6a269a6eb0c5ed8e1d07153f311110ed9922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 09:58:47 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] cpuidle: psci: create the cpuidle device after deferred
 probing

With OSI, the CPU PM domains are created by a platform driver that
defers until every parent domain's provider has probed. When the
outermost one is the Qualcomm MPM, which waits on its mailbox and the
RPM, the domains only appear after device_initcall. The psci-cpuidle
faux device can't defer, so it failed to attach CPU 0 and the CPUs were
left without cpuidle at all.

Create it at late_initcall_sync, once deferred probing is done.

Signed-off-by: Lars Wikman <lars@underjord.io>
---
 drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c | 6 +++++-
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
index dcf20ea..0d52e80 100644
--- a/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
+++ b/drivers/cpuidle/cpuidle-psci.c
@@ -489,4 +489,8 @@ static int __init psci_idle_init(void)
 
 	return 0;
 }
-device_initcall(psci_idle_init);
+/*
+ * The CPU PM domains can hang off a provider probed late, such as the
+ * Qualcomm MPM, and the faux device can't defer: wait for deferred probes.
+ */
+late_initcall_sync(psci_idle_init);
-- 
